  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified specification uses only task-level search, approach, claim, release, pickup, drop, publication, color-observation, operation-result, and team-reception events needed for the complex delivery objective. Low-level movement and obstacle events are omitted because obstacle response is already enforced by collision_avoidance and the objective forbids adding low-level mission decisions.",
    "transition_design": "The select_RGB through select_none states track colors unavailable through received claims or delivery reports and restore released colors. A color is claimed only after its object-visible observation. A competing claim before the first successful pickup leads through release_R, release_G, or release_B. After claiming, object and zone search or approach actions are repeatable only in their corresponding phases, visibility loss returns to search, and reached observations gate pickup and drop. Pickup and delivery failures retry the unchanged cycle. Red executes three one-box cycles, green executes two batches of up to two boxes, and blue executes one batch of up to three boxes. Publication is enabled only after the color's third box has been delivered. R_complete, G_complete, and B_complete are stable local completion checkpoints; synchronized marking with team_delivery_status_plant_corrected occurs only when all three colors are delivered.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
  }
}
